# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Mina lightnet nginx config.
# Used when NGINX_TEMPLATE=mina.conf.template (dedicated Mina lightnet box).
# Proxies:
#   mina.DOMAIN/graphql        → local mina-lightnet:3085 (GraphQL)
#   mina-accounts.DOMAIN       → local mina-lightnet:8181 (accounts manager)
#
# Like devnet.conf.template (see its header), backends are named through a
# VARIABLE plus the Docker embedded resolver rather than as literal hostnames,
# so nginx boots even if `mina-lightnet` is briefly down and re-resolves it per
# request after a recreate. This file was the one template on this box still
# using the literal form; #1013 brought it in line. A literal upstream that is
# not running at parse time is `[emerg] host not found in upstream`, which
# exits the whole nginx master — including the port-80 ACME block — and a
# lightnet is exactly the kind of container that is sometimes down.
#
# The `proxy_pass` lines carry NO URI part: with a variable upstream nginx does
# not do the literal form's prefix substitution (issue #987), so the request
# `$uri` is forwarded as-is. Both locations wanted that already — `location
# /graphql` proxied to `.../graphql`, an identity — so no `rewrite` is needed.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=rpc:10m rate=30r/s;

server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name mina.${DOMAIN} mina-accounts.${DOMAIN};

    location /.well-known/acme-challenge/ {
        root /var/www/certbot;
    }
    location / {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
}

# GraphQL endpoint for the Mina lightnet
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    http2 on;
    server_name mina.${DOMAIN};

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/mina.${DOMAIN}/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/mina.${DOMAIN}/privkey.pem;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=10s ipv6=off;

    location /graphql {
        limit_req zone=rpc burst=60 nodelay;
        set $upstream mina-lightnet;
        proxy_pass http://$upstream:3085;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
        client_max_body_size 4m;
    }
    location / { return 404; }
}

# Accounts manager — lets clients acquire pre-funded Mina devnet accounts
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    http2 on;
    server_name mina-accounts.${DOMAIN};

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/mina.${DOMAIN}/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/mina.${DOMAIN}/privkey.pem;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=10s ipv6=off;

    location / {
        limit_req zone=rpc burst=20 nodelay;
        set $upstream mina-lightnet;
        proxy_pass http://$upstream:8181;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_read_timeout 30s;
    }
}
